TEXT 248 32 Left 2 ;The R(f) is derived from a 3*635mm2 (RDC=0.01438ohm) overhead line from ATP\nThis function is than approximated by a rational function\noptimized by CurveExpert. \nThe formula is  y=a+b*d**freq+c*freq (works till 10kHz)\nFor other lines with other RDC the formula is related to the RDC of the line above\nI've not tried yet if this makes any sense\nbut i've also no idea how the R(f) of a netimpedance (lines,transformers) \ncan be derived otherwise better\nThe result is, i thin, somehow more qualitative than quantitative
TEXT 72 -160 Left 2 ;Netimpedance ohmic\npart with\nskineffect
