TEXT 184 -160 Left 2 ;Netimpedance\n inductive part
TEXT -80 -400 Left 5 ;Simple simulation of the skin effect (qualitative)\n=====================================\n( The skin resistance is altered via a given external frequency value )
TEXT 248 128 Left 2 ;To the skin effect:\nThe resistance is here a part 50Hz and another part 1470Hz\nThe high frequency part always decrease and the 50Hz part will be stronger.\nTherefore the skin effect is more iterative as constant (like modelled here)\nSo the real current is somehow between the shapes of the current without skineffect\nand the current with skin effect. \nIf the circuit has more than one resonant frequencies it is even more complicated\nto model the skin effect. \nIt may be possible to get some skin dependent resistances in series with different length (sum=full length)\nand different skin frequencies and also a resistance part of 50Hz.
